  "name": "Dray Container Hauler",
  "description": "A container hauler: a long hold for fourteen 20-foot containers with an overhead crane down its length and a well in its belly to lift them through, a small crew section forward and a drive room aft. Two big torch drives push it, each with its own engine in the drive room behind it, and attitude jets at the bow and stern move it about. It stands on six long legs over a container, opens its well and lifts the box up into its hold; lift jets hold it up, loaded, and its containers ride in three frozen cargo volumes.",
